/* (longshot) Every switch the game reads (host/ and gpu/vk; not eden, sirit or third_party), one line each:

     SWITCH(NAME, TYPE, SCOPE, "area", "what")

   TYPE   FLAG (env_on: unset, 0, false, off or no is off), INT, FLOAT, TEXT, PATH (a file or folder), or ANY (not said yet)
   SCOPE  GAME: may be set in longshot_env.txt, the file players pass around (host/hos_main.c env_line_allowed)
          LOCAL: from the environment (or HOS_ENV_FILE) only: it names a file or folder, or presses buttons on a timer
          SYSTEM: the system's or a library's variable, which the game reads but does not own
   area   the file that reads it (the first, where several do)
   what   what it does, in a sentence; "" until someone says (the docs' tables have the rest)

   tests/test_switch_list.py fails when a switch is read and not listed here, or listed and read nowhere:
   `python -I scripts/switch_list.py --update` adds the line (its type where the reads make it certain) and drops the old
   one; then say what it does. A C or C++ file that wants the list defines SWITCH(name, type, scope, area, what) and
   includes this file. */
SWITCH(APPIMAGE, ANY, SYSTEM, "gpu/vk/vk_bug_report.cpp", "")
